# Post-deploy Inngest sync

## Problem

ai-hero deploys do not sync their Inngest function manifest. Every push auto-deploys and aliases in ~2 minutes, but the Inngest registration is only refreshed when a human remembers to `curl -X PUT https://www.aihero.dev/api/inngest`. New or renamed functions therefore register late or never — the "dead binding" failure mode.

Receipts:
- 2026-07-20: system-bus reconciler dead-bound after a deploy; recovered by manual PUT.
- 2026-07-21: same on ai-hero after the confirmation-reconciler shipped; recovered by manual PUT.
- 2026-07-24: ~10 deploys since the 07-21 registration; a manual PUT returned `modified:true`, confirming the manifest had drifted the whole time.

## What to build

A post-deploy step that issues the registration PUT against the production deployment automatically, on every production deploy, and **fails loudly** if the PUT does not return success. Investigate the repo's existing deploy pipeline first (Vercel project settings, GitHub Actions in `.github/workflows/`, any `vercel.json` hooks) and choose the mechanism that fits what is already there — do not invent a parallel pipeline.

Requirements:
- Runs only for production deploys, not previews.
- Idempotent and safe to re-run.
- Its output must be findable later: log the response (`modified` true/false) where a human can see it in the deploy record.
- Registration success is NOT proof of health — note in the implementation (comment or doc) that run-recency assertion is the real check, owned by a separate joelclaw-side step.

## Deliverable

The change, plus a short written explanation of where it hooks in and how to verify it fired on the next real deploy. **Do not deploy.** Steering reviews and commits; the first real verification happens on the next natural push.

## Constraints

- Do NOT commit, do NOT push, do NOT deploy, do NOT trigger a build.
- Do not add secrets to the repo. If the mechanism needs a token or env var, state exactly which one and where it must be set — never inline a value, never print an existing one.
- This checkout may sit on a foreign branch with other sessions' work — check `git status` first, touch only your own files, and report what you found.
- If a command is BLOCKED by dcg, stop and report it.
- Print a DONE summary when finished.
